OpenMagicka fork: an interactive cue threw its sound away and started a new one whenever its
variable changed at all, even when the value still chose the same variation. Magicka's steam spray
is interactive on OrientationAngle, which every 3D placement changes, so it restarted every tick
(a sawtooth buzz), and once stopping its release started over each time and never ended. The
sound now changes only when another variation is chosen, and not at all once the cue is stopping.

diff --git a/src/FACT_internal.c b/src/FACT_internal.c
index 1cdb334..5a9d91a 100644
--- a/src/FACT_internal.c
+++ b/src/FACT_internal.c
@@ -1634,8 +1634,20 @@ static void FACT_INTERNAL_UpdateCue(FACTCue *cue)
 		}
 		if (next != cue->interactive)
 		{
+			uint16_t variationIndex;
 			cue->interactive = next;
 
+			/* OpenMagicka fork: the sound changes only when the value
+			 * chooses another variation, and never once the cue is
+			 * stopping (its release would start over and never end). */
+			if (	(cue->state & FACT_STATE_STOPPING) ||
+				(	cue->playingSound != NULL &&
+					get_active_variation_index(cue, &variationIndex) &&
+					variationIndex == cue->playingSound->variation_index	)	)
+			{
+				return;
+			}
+
 			/* New sound, time for death! */
 			if (cue->playingSound != NULL)
 			{
